From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:08:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Breath of the Wild above 60 fps and above 1080p
 (seedds/nxnative#76)

seedds/nxnative#76 at 0f2a772c, rebased onto the fork's pin (ee6648cb) and its patch series. The rewriter table of a
Breath of the Wild 1.9.0 build names further stubs (VAR_STEP, RENDER_POOL, VIEW_W / VIEW_H, OUTPUT_W / OUTPUT_H). The loader
writes the state page fields from +0x40 on only for such a build. DM_FPS_TARGET 61 to 240 gives a variable frame step, and
any build without VAR_STEP refuses it. DM_RENDER_SCALE above 1.0 (up to 3.0) grows the render buffer pool, the application
pool and the alias region, on the Mac only. Menus, held buttons and the physics step follow the frame ratio.

Adapted to the fork: hle_svc.c and loader.c read the profile through dm_profile() (runtime-profile patch) instead of the
DM_GAME_* macros. The generated docs/agents/game-patches.md and docs/agents/symptoms.md are left to patches.py apply.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#76
Reason: Breath of the Wild above 60 fps and above 1080p on the Mac until upstream merges it
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#287
